      "body": "## Motivation\n\nThe small-row speculative argmax and DSpark fused Markov greedy step select indices using equality with a reduced maximum. NaN scores can leave an invalid or incorrect index: on H100, an all-NaN row of width 131072 returns 131072, and the Markov kernel at width 152064 returns INT_MAX. Passing such a token to the next embedding lookup can cause a device-side failure.\n\n## Modifications\n\nGive NaNs priority and select the first index, matching `torch.argmax`. Exclude padded lanes from candidate indices. The row kernel keeps separate value/index reductions with NaN propagation; the final reduction and Markov kernels reuse the existing NaN-aware `_argmax_pair` helper. This does not repair the source of NaNs or make an affected request's output valid.\n\nOnly two kernel files change; no new test files.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nLocal H100 PCIe, PyTorch 2.14.1+cu130, baseline `a99c7d050f`:\n\n- 333 direct GPU comparisons against PyTorch: finite values, all/partial NaNs, positive/negative infinities, ties, strided rows, vocabulary/tile boundaries, and NaNs originating in the Markov matvec. Baseline failed 96 cases; patched kernels pass all 333. Markov matvec cases include FP32/BF16/FP16; finite winners are separated to exclude the kernel's documented near-tie rounding differences.\n- 16 CUDA graph replays with changed NaN locations, followed by embedding lookups, pass. Includes the all-NaN width-131072 case.\n- Ruff lint/format and `git diff --check` pass.\n\nThese are kernel-level checks with constructed exceptional inputs, not a reproduction of spontaneous NaNs in a running model.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNormal-input CUDA graph microbenchmark, vocabulary 152064, median of five samples (16 calls per graph, 100 replays per sample). This correctness fix has a measurable cost in the small-row argmax; these numbers do not establish an end-to-end serving impact.\n\n| Kernel | Before (µs) | After (µs) |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| row_argmax, 1 row | 3.46 | 3.66 |\n| row_argmax, 16 rows | 7.06 | 8.84 |\n| row_argmax, 64 rows | 20.69 | 26.26 |\n| Markov, 1 row, rank 32 | 9.59 | 9.51 |\n| Markov, 1 row, rank 128 | 62.45 | 62.34 |\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40202292236](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40202292236)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40202292230](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40202292230)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40202292200](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40202292200)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
